Feb 18, 2026 v1.5

What's Changed

Added

Added saved colors management with the saved command.
Added persistent storage for saved colors in:
~/.config/wl-color-picker/colors
Added graphical interface for viewing saved colors.
Added ability to reopen and edit saved colors.
Added ability to delete individual saved colors.
Added ability to clear all saved colors.
Added duplicate prevention when saving colors.
Added hexadecimal color validation and normalization to uppercase #RRGGBB.
Added support for selecting colors through a graphical YAD color editor.
Added a graphical main menu when no command is specified.
Added automatic creation of the configuration directory and colors file.
Added separate dependency handling for the saved command.
Added support for ImageMagick through the magick command in addition to GraphicsMagick.
Added gettext-based internationalization.
Added localized fallback messages when gettext is unavailable.
Added Ukrainian (uk) language support.
Added localized fallback messages for Portuguese, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Japanese, Russian, Chinese, and Ukrainian.
Added improved error handling for missing dependencies.
Added graceful handling of cancelled color selection and color editing dialogs.
Added cleanup of temporary screenshot files after color extraction.

Changed

Saved colors are now normalized before being stored.
The saved command no longer requires slurp, grim, or ImageMagick/GraphicsMagick.
Color extraction now supports both GraphicsMagick and ImageMagick.
Improved error reporting through YAD when available, with terminal fallback otherwise.

Internationalization

Added gettext domain configuration for wl-color-picker.
Added support for localized interface strings through:
/usr/share/locale
Added Ukrainian (uk) to the supported languages.


